Build nvidia-drm and the open nvidia-uvm on Linux 7.4.

Backport of NVIDIA/open-gpu-kernel-modules PR #1414 (open, unmerged; written
against 615.71.09): https://github.com/NVIDIA/open-gpu-kernel-modules/pull/1414
  29bb7233e4c8 nvidia-drm: Support plane atomic state creation
  9c66f3b92569 nvidia-drm: Support CRTC atomic state creation
  3d8e17b7162d nvidia-drm: Handle the relocated fbdev helper header
    -> kernel/ and kernel-module-source/kernel-open/
  7a479a2474af nvidia-uvm: Replace the removed VM_SPECIAL mask
  d5e1c19d63dc nvidia-uvm: Detect the renamed hugetlb VMA helper
    -> kernel-module-source/kernel-open/ only (580's proprietary uvm_hmm.c
       is a stub)
ad314a95b7a3 (dmem region init) is not needed: 580 has no dmem code.

Changes for 580.196.07: the new conftest cases follow memory_device_coherent
(580's case order differs), and the plane state is allocated with
nv_drm_calloc() as 580's reset hook does (580 has no
nv_drm_plane_state_alloc(), and keeps degamma_multiplier at 0).
